  <reporting-org ref="GB-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK - Foreign, Commonwealth Development Office (FCDO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NRC- Improvement of Protection of Internal Displaced People (IDP) Through Provision of Civil Documentation in Cabo Delgado</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of this project is to support Internal Displaced People (IDP) to obtain civil documentation, which a significant portion of the IDP population lacks. The envisaged outcome is that 20,000 IDPs will gain access to legal identity documents through strengthening of awareness around the processes for document issuance (legal awareness), provision of counselling and assistance related to document issuance processes, and facilitation of civil documentation for IDPs. The sustainable impact of possession of national IDs and birth certificates provided to communities will enable key rights-based improved access to services, freedom of movement, and legal recognition before the law.</narrative>
  </description>
